++### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs (Workspace Settings)
++
++- **name:** Internal database name representing the workspace tenant in PostgreSQL. Required during bootstrap and immutable across standard operation, binding the tenant scope for Row-Level Security policies.
++- **slug:** URL-safe ASCII slug identifying the tenant in REST API endpoints (`/api/v1/workspaces/{slug}`) and browser URL routes (`/{slug}/projects`). Must be between 2 and 63 alphanumeric characters and hyphens.
++- **display_name:** The human-facing label rendered on topbars, page document titles, mobile shells, and notification cards. Supports UTF-8 strings up to 80 characters with full internationalization.
++- **default_project_visibility:** Sets the default privacy tier assigned when users create new projects. Options are `"workspace"` (visible to all authenticated workspace members) or `"private"` (accessible strictly to explicitly invited members and project administrators).
++- **session_idle_timeout_min:** Controls how long an idle user session remains active before requiring step-up authentication or PIN challenge. Configurable from 5 minutes to 720 minutes (12 hours), with a standard enterprise default of 60 minutes.
++- **session_absolute_timeout_min:** Maximum wall-clock lifespan of an authenticated session cookie regardless of user activity. Must fall between 60 minutes (1 hour) and 10080 minutes (7 days), defaulting to 1440 minutes (24 hours).
++- **trash_retention_days:** Defines how many days soft-deleted work items, docs, stickies, and cycles reside in the Trash Studio (`/trash`) before being permanently purged by the background vacuum worker. Values range from 7 to 365 days (default 30 days).
++- **mcp_key_max_ttl_days:** Upper boundary enforced when administrators or developers mint Model Context Protocol (MCP) scoped tokens. The backend rejects any key creation request specifying a TTL exceeding this configured cap (1 to 365 days, default 90 days).
++- **air_gap_mode:** When set to `true`, 👍kanban activates zero-external-egress enforcement. All outbound requests to cloud AI providers (OpenAI, Gemini) and remote webhooks are fail-closed blocked at the transport layer, restricting agent pipelines exclusively to LAN Ollama servers and local CLI runners.
++- **default_skip_loaded_sequence_numbers:** An optimization flag for high-throughput teams. When enabled, WebSocket clients receiving state updates skip downloading historical activity sequence packets that the client has already recorded in IndexedDB.
++- **issue_export_enabled:** Master toggle for work item data extraction. Disabling this flag blocks `/api/v1/projects/{project}/issues/export` across both the REST API and the web interface to prevent bulk data exfiltration.
++- **issue_export_allowed_roles:** Role allowlist determining who can trigger issue exports. Configurable with combinations of `"workspace_admin"`, `"project_admin"`, and `"member"`.
++- **issue_import_enabled:** Administrative toggle governing data ingestion from external platforms (Plane, Jira, GitHub, Linear). Disabling this blocks `/api/v1/admin/imports` to preserve data integrity during audit periods.
++- **report_export_enabled:** Controls whether statistical flow telemetry, Monte Carlo lead-time forecasts, and velocity percentiles can be downloaded as CSV or JSON payloads.
++- **report_export_allowed_roles:** Specifies the minimum permission tier required to export engineering flow reports (options include `"ADMIN"` and `"MEMBER"`).
++
++### Step-by-Step Guide: Configuring Workspace Policies and Trash Retention
++
++1. **Access Workspace Settings:** Click your avatar or the settings cog in the top navigation bar and select **Workspace Settings** (or navigate directly to `/workspaces/<slug>/settings`).
++2. **Review General Policies:** In the **General** tab, update your **Display Name**, verify the **Workspace Slug**, and select the **Default Project Visibility** (`Workspace` or `Private`).
++3. **Configure Session Security:**
++   - Under **Session Lifetimes**, set **Session Idle Timeout** (e.g. 60 minutes) to force re-authentication for unattended terminals.
++   - Set **Session Absolute Timeout** (e.g. 1440 minutes / 24 hours) to mandate periodic credential rotation.
++4. **Tune Compliance & Trash Retention:**
++   - Navigate to the **Data Lifecycle & Trash** card.
++   - Adjust **Trash Retention Days** between 7 and 365 days (default 30 days).
++   - Soft-deleted work items remain recoverable in `/trash` for this duration. Once this window elapses, the automated cleanup daemon purges the records irreversibly.
++5. **Manage Air-Gap and Export Restrictions:**
++   - If operating in a sovereign or disconnected environment, toggle **Air-Gap Mode** to `ON` to strictly restrict all agent and runner execution to LAN hosts.
++   - Review **Allowed Export Roles** to ensure only authorized administrators and team leads can extract bulk project archives.
++6. **Save Changes:** Click **`Save Settings`**. Changes are validated, logged in the immutable audit ledger, and take effect across the workspace immediately.
