++### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs (Workflow Transition Studio & Repo Bindings)
++
++- **name:** The user-defined identifier assigned to the workflow hook (such as `qa-done-gate` or `enforce-pr-link`). Appears on pipeline transition cards, dry-run evaluation outputs, and timeline rejection entries.
++- **from_state:** The initial state of the card before transition (e.g. `In Progress`). Selecting `null` creates a wildcard rule matching transitions originating from any state into `to_state`.
++- **to_state:** The protected destination state (e.g. `Done`). The card cannot land in this state until all attached synchronous validators pass and all asynchronous agent gates approve.
++- **hook_kind:** Defines the execution engine: `"sync_validator"` runs fast in-process WebAssembly checks (<25ms); `"sync_mutator"` applies deterministic property updates; `"agent_interceptor"` dispatches an asynchronous background gate to an AI model or test runner.
++- **failure_policy:** The error handling invariant. `"fail_closed"` (default) blocks the transition immediately if the helper fails, times out, or errors. `"fail_open"` logs an administrative warning to the activity ledger and allows the card transition to complete.
++- **wasm_module_sha256:** The cryptographic hash of the compiled WebAssembly bytecode module executed by the `wasmtime` engine. Prevents execution of unverified or tampered binaries.
++- **agent:** The slug of the registered autonomous agent (`@reality-checker`, `@security-auditor`) assigned to evaluate asynchronous gate transitions. The attach dialog groups available agents by execution harness (`cli_pipe`, `in_app_sdk`, `remote_runner`).
++- **timeout_ms:** The maximum wall-clock execution deadline allocated to the helper. For Wasm validators, timeouts are capped at 250ms. For agent interceptors, timeouts can be configured up to 60000ms (60 seconds) to accommodate large reasoning model evaluations.
++- **allowed_mutable_fields:** A strict security allowlist restricting which issue properties a `sync_mutator` hook can modify (e.g. `closed_at`, `labels`, `priority`). Project invariants strictly forbid modifying `state` or `description_markdown` to prevent recursive transition loops and content tampering.
++- **repo_slug:** The local filesystem folder name allocated to the bare Git mirror. Must be a clean lowercase alphanumeric string with hyphens.
++- **remote_url:** The external Git repository URL (e.g. `https://github.com/org/repo.git`). The server validates the URL against an anti-SSRF policy (blocking RFC 1918 private IP addresses unless explicitly allowlisted) before establishing outbound connections.
++- **default_branch:** The primary branch name against which code inspection scripts, PR validation checks, and diff analyses are evaluated.
++- **sync_interval_min:** Interval in minutes between background mirror fetch operations. The daemon executes `git fetch --prune` inside the bare mirror to maintain parity with remote pushes.
++
++### Step-by-Step Guide: Attaching Workflow Transition Hooks with Dry-Run
++
++1. **Navigate to Workflow Studio:** Open `/projects/<PROJECT_KEY>/settings/workflows`.
++2. **Select Transition Rule:** Locate the transition rule card for your target state movement (e.g. `In Progress -> Done`).
++3. **Click Attach Hook:** Click the **`+ Attach Hook`** button to open the **Attach Workflow Hook Dialog**.
++4. **Define Hook Parameters:**
++   - **Name:** Enter a unique label (e.g. `reality-checker-done-gate`).
++   - **Hook Kind:** Select `sync_validator` (Wasm), `sync_mutator` (Wasm), or `agent_interceptor` (Async Agent Gate).
++   - **Failure Policy:** Choose `Fail-Closed` to guarantee that unverified tickets cannot enter the protected state.
++5. **Select Engine or Agent:**
++   - For Wasm: Choose an approved module (e.g. `check-blockers-resolved`).
++   - For Agent Interceptor: Select the target **Agent Definition** from the dropdown. The system automatically reads the agent's real `timeout_ms` (e.g. `60000ms`).
++6. **Save Hook:** Click **`Attach Hook`** to commit the hook to the project's transition pipeline.
++7. **Simulate in Dry-Run Drawer:**
++   - Click the **`Dry-Run`** button on the rule card.
++   - Choose a sample ticket fixture or enter a live issue key.
++   - Click **`Run Dry-Run`** to execute the pipeline in a simulated, non-mutating sandbox.
++   - Inspect the execution timings (e.g. `1.2ms`, `3.4ms`), returned logs, and allowed/vetoed verdicts before deploying to production.
++
++### Step-by-Step Guide: Binding Git Repositories
++
++1. **Access Repository Bindings:** Navigate to `/projects/<PROJECT_KEY>/settings/workflows` and scroll down to the **Git Repository Bindings** section.
++2. **Click Add Repository:** Click **`+ Add Repository`** to open the repository configuration drawer.
++3. **Configure Repository Details:**
++   - **Slug:** Provide a clean identifier (e.g. `kanban-core`).
++   - **Remote URL:** Enter the remote Git repository URL.
++   - **Default Branch:** Enter the default branch (`main`).
++   - **Sync Interval:** Configure the automated polling frequency (default 15 minutes).
++4. **Enforce Read-Only Mirror Invariant:** The system creates a local bare Git mirror with strict read-only permissions (`:ro`). Autonomous agents can query commit trees and run `git diff` during gate reviews, but write access is impossible.
++5. **Trigger Immediate Sync:** Click **`Sync Now`** to perform an initial clone and verify that commit SHAs and branch references synchronize successfully.
