-    "content": "# [Architectural] Admin Custom Scripted Fields and Sandboxed Execution\n\n## Overview\n\nModern software development requires dynamic metadata: calculated story points, security compliance flags, release readiness scores, and SLA countdowns. However, permitting custom scripts to run inside a project management system has historically introduced catastrophic security vulnerabilities, including server-side request forgery (SSRF), infinite loops, and arbitrary code execution.\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban resolves this through **Admin-Only Custom Scripted Fields** evaluated inside a hardened, multi-tier isolation sandbox with cryptographic privilege escalation controls.\n\n---\n\n## Admin-Only Definition Security Gate\n\nTo protect the platform from unauthorized logic injection:\n- **Admin-Only Gate:** Only verified Server Administrators or Project Administrators possessing Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2) credentials can create, modify, or delete custom field scripts.\n- **Route Protection:** All custom field endpoints under `/api/v1/projects/{project_id}/custom-fields` declare explicit dependencies on `require_admin_aal2`.\n- **Immutable Script Signatures:** When a script is saved, a SHA-256 cryptographic digest is generated and recorded. Any unauthorized database tampering immediately invalidates script execution.\n\n---\n\n## The Custom Fields Studio\n\nAdministrators manage custom fields through the visual studio at `/projects/KAN/settings/custom-fields`.\n\n![Custom Fields Studio and Escalation Banner](images/14-custom-fields-studio.png)\n\n### Studio Capabilities\n- **Field Types:** String, Integer, Float, Boolean, Date, Multi-Select, and Dynamic Computed Script.\n- **Execution Engine Selection:** Choose between lightweight WebAssembly (Wasmtime) or isolated containerized scripts (nsjail).\n- **Execution Badging (`\ud83e\uddea`):** Computed fields render a subtle test tube (`\ud83e\uddea`) glyph on the ticket properties rail, showing real-time computation status and latency.\n- **Pre-Commit Test Execution:** Test custom script logic against sample payloads in real time before committing field definitions to the database.\n\n---\n\n## Test-Execute Sandbox Modal\n\nBefore saving or deploying a custom scripted field to production tickets, administrators can validate script logic in an interactive test execution modal:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Admin as Project Admin (AAL2)\n    participant Studio as Custom Fields Studio\n    participant Modal as Test-Execute Modal\n    participant Sandbox as Wasm / nsjail Sandbox\n\n    Admin->>Studio: Author script source (e.g. CVSS calculation)\n    Admin->>Studio: Click \"Test-Execute\"\n    Studio->>Modal: Open Test-Execute Modal with sample ticket JSON\n    Admin->>Modal: Click \"Run Test\"\n    Modal->>Sandbox: Execute script against sample properties\n    Sandbox-->>Modal: Return evaluated output, execution time (<2ms), stdout logs\n    Modal-->>Admin: Render live severity pill preview (e.g. \"8.8 High\")\n```\n\n![Custom Fields Pre-Commit Test Execution Modal](images/53-custom-fields-test-execute.png)\n\nThe Test-Execute modal displays execution duration, memory consumption, output formatting, and sandboxed stdout logs. This guarantees that syntax errors, infinite loops, or unexpected outputs are caught before fields impact active workflows.\n\n---\n\n## Multi-Tier Execution Sandbox Architecture\n\nWhen a work item is created or updated, active custom field scripts are executed within an isolated multi-tier sandbox:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Update[\"Work Item Updated: State / Properties Changed\"] --> Dispatcher[\"Sandbox Dispatcher (kanban/sandbox/)\"]\n    \n    Dispatcher -->|Lightweight Math / String Formats| TierA[\"Tier A: Wasmtime Engine<br/>- In-process WebAssembly<br/>- Sub-millisecond execution (<1ms)<br/>- Zero OS syscall capability<br/>- Memory capped at 16 MB\"]\n    Dispatcher -->|Complex Logic / Scripts| TierB[\"Tier B: nsjail Container Jail<br/>- Linux namespaces (CLONE_NEWNET)<br/>- Read-only root filesystem<br/>- CPU timeout: 5 sec, Memory: 512 MB\"]\n    \n    TierA --> Verify[\"Verify Computed Value vs Pydantic Schema\"]\n    TierB --> Verify\n    Verify --> Store[\"Recorded in work item properties JSONB\"]\n```\n\n![Custom Fields on Ticket Properties Rail](images/36-rail-custom-fields.png)\n\n### Tier A: WebAssembly Runtime (Wasmtime)\n- Runs compiled WebAssembly modules in-process.\n- Provides sub-millisecond execution times.\n- Zero capability to open sockets, access the filesystem, or spawn processes.\n- Memory allocation strictly capped at 16 MB with instruction count fuel limits.\n\n### Tier B: Hardened Container Jail (nsjail)\n- Utilizes Linux kernel namespaces (`CLONE_NEWPID`, `CLONE_NEWNET`, `CLONE_NEWNS`).\n- Root filesystem mounted strictly read-only.\n- Network access completely disabled (`CLONE_NEWNET`).\n- Hard resource limits enforced via cgroups (512 MB RAM, 5-second wall clock timeout).\n\n---\n\n## Ephemeral Scoped Tokens and Tiered Privilege Escalation\n\nCustom scripts often need to query project metadata (such as counting open bugs or reading cycle end dates). To prevent privilege leakage:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Script as Custom Scripted Field\n    participant Gate as Authorization Gate\n    participant Admin as Server/Workspace Admin (AAL2)\n    participant TokenService as Ephemeral Token Minter\n\n    Note over Script,TokenService: Default Execution: Project Scoped\n    Script->>Gate: Execute with default Project-scoped ephemeral token\n    \n    Note over Script,TokenService: Escalation Request: Workspace or Server\n    Script->>Gate: Request Escalated Scope (WORKSPACE or SERVER)\n    Gate->>Admin: Display Unmissable Blast Radius Warning Banner\n    Admin->>Gate: Cryptographic Signature with AAL2 Confirmation\n    Gate->>TokenService: Mint Time-Limited Ephemeral Escalated Token\n    TokenService-->>Script: Deliver Ephemeral Token for Execution\n```\n\n1. **Ephemeral Project Tokens:** By default, every script executes using an ephemeral API token scoped strictly to the current **Project**. It cannot read data from other projects or workspace settings.\n2. **Cryptographic Privilege Escalation:** If a script requires broader access (such as reading data across the entire **Workspace** or querying **Server** configuration):\n   - The script must request an escalated token scope.\n   - The UI displays an unmissable administrative warning banner detailing the blast radius.\n   - The escalation must be signed with cryptographic approval by an administrator possessing authority over that target tier.\n   - Scripts can never escalate to Server Admin privileges without explicit multi-factor confirmation.\n\n![Custom Fields Dual Control Escalation Studio](images/52-custom-fields-dual-control.png)\n\n### Dual-Control Principle:\nTo satisfy enterprise SOC 2 and ISO 27001 separation of duties, escalating a custom scripted field to workspace-wide or server-wide scope requires dual-control authorization:\n- A project administrator can author and propose the escalation.\n- A distinct, independent administrator holding target tier authority must review the blast radius warning banner and supply fresh Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2) credentials to activate the escalated token scope.\n- All escalation grants are logged with SHA-256 cryptographic digests in the immutable audit ledger.\n"
+    "content": "# [Architectural] Admin Custom Scripted Fields and Sandboxed Execution\n\n## Overview\n\nModern software development requires dynamic metadata: calculated story points, security compliance flags, release readiness scores, and SLA countdowns. However, permitting custom scripts to run inside a project management system has historically introduced catastrophic security vulnerabilities, including server-side request forgery (SSRF), infinite loops, and arbitrary code execution.\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban resolves this through **Admin-Only Custom Scripted Fields** evaluated inside a hardened, multi-tier isolation sandbox with cryptographic privilege escalation controls.\n\n---\n\n## Admin-Only Definition Security Gate\n\nTo protect the platform from unauthorized logic injection:\n- **Admin-Only Gate:** Only verified Server Administrators or Project Administrators possessing Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2) credentials can create, modify, or delete custom field scripts.\n- **Route Protection:** All custom field endpoints under `/api/v1/projects/{project_id}/custom-fields` declare explicit dependencies on `require_admin_aal2`.\n- **Immutable Script Signatures:** When a script is saved, a SHA-256 cryptographic digest is generated and recorded. Any unauthorized database tampering immediately invalidates script execution.\n\n---\n\n## The Custom Fields Studio\n\nAdministrators manage custom fields through the visual studio at `/projects/KAN/settings/custom-fields`.\n\n![Custom Fields Studio and Escalation Banner](images/slice5-custom-fields-studio-desktop-1440x900-light.png)\n\n### Studio Capabilities\n- **Field Types:** String, Integer, Float, Boolean, Date, Multi-Select, and Dynamic Computed Script.\n- **Execution Engine Selection:** Choose between lightweight WebAssembly (Wasmtime) or isolated containerized scripts (nsjail).\n- **Execution Badging (`\ud83e\uddea`):** Computed fields render a subtle test tube (`\ud83e\uddea`) glyph on the ticket properties rail, showing real-time computation status and latency.\n- **Pre-Commit Test Execution:** Test custom script logic against sample payloads in real time before committing field definitions to the database.\n\n![Custom Fields Editor Tier A](images/slice5-custom-fields-editor-tier-a-desktop-1440x900-light.png)\n\n---\n\n## Test-Execute Sandbox Modal\n\nBefore saving or deploying a custom scripted field to production tickets, administrators can validate script logic in an interactive test execution modal:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Admin as Project Admin (AAL2)\n    participant Studio as Custom Fields Studio\n    participant Modal as Test-Execute Modal\n    participant Sandbox as Wasm / nsjail Sandbox\n\n    Admin->>Studio: Author script source (e.g. CVSS calculation)\n    Admin->>Studio: Click \"Test-Execute\"\n    Studio->>Modal: Open Test-Execute Modal with sample ticket JSON\n    Admin->>Modal: Click \"Run Test\"\n    Modal->>Sandbox: Execute script against sample properties\n    Sandbox-->>Modal: Return evaluated output, execution time (<2ms), stdout logs\n    Modal-->>Admin: Render live severity pill preview (e.g. \"8.8 High\")\n```\n\n![Custom Fields Pre-Commit Test Execution Modal](images/53-custom-fields-test-execute.png)\n\nThe Test-Execute modal displays execution duration, memory consumption, output formatting, and sandboxed stdout logs. This guarantees that syntax errors, infinite loops, or unexpected outputs are caught before fields impact active workflows.\n\n---\n\n## Multi-Tier Execution Sandbox Architecture\n\nWhen a work item is created or updated, active custom field scripts are executed within an isolated multi-tier sandbox:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Update[\"Work Item Updated: State / Properties Changed\"] --> Dispatcher[\"Sandbox Dispatcher (kanban/sandbox/)\"]\n    \n    Dispatcher -->|Lightweight Math / String Formats| TierA[\"Tier A: Wasmtime Engine - In-process WebAssembly - Sub-millisecond execution (<1ms) - Zero OS syscall capability - Memory capped at 16 MB\"]\n    Dispatcher -->|Complex Logic / Scripts| TierB[\"Tier B: nsjail Container Jail - Linux namespaces (CLONE_NEWNET) - Read-only root filesystem - CPU timeout: 5 sec, Memory: 512 MB\"]\n    \n    TierA --> Verify[\"Verify Computed Value vs Pydantic Schema\"]\n    TierB --> Verify\n    Verify --> Store[\"Recorded in work item properties JSONB\"]\n```\n\n![Custom Fields on Ticket Properties Rail](images/36-rail-custom-fields.png)\n\n### Tier A: WebAssembly Runtime (Wasmtime)\n- Runs compiled WebAssembly modules in-process.\n- Provides sub-millisecond execution times.\n- Zero capability to open sockets, access the filesystem, or spawn processes.\n- Memory allocation strictly capped at 16 MB with instruction count fuel limits.\n\n### Tier B: Hardened Container Jail (nsjail)\n- Utilizes Linux kernel namespaces (`CLONE_NEWPID`, `CLONE_NEWNET`, `CLONE_NEWNS`).\n- Root filesystem mounted strictly read-only.\n- Network access completely disabled (`CLONE_NEWNET`).\n- Hard resource limits enforced via cgroups (512 MB RAM, 5-second wall clock timeout).\n\n---\n\n## Ephemeral Scoped Tokens and Tiered Privilege Escalation\n\nCustom scripts often need to query project metadata (such as counting open bugs or reading cycle end dates). To prevent privilege leakage:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Script as Custom Scripted Field\n    participant Gate as Authorization Gate\n    participant Admin as Server/Workspace Admin (AAL2)\n    participant TokenService as Ephemeral Token Minter\n\n    Note over Script,TokenService: Default Execution: Project Scoped\n    Script->>Gate: Execute with default Project-scoped ephemeral token\n    \n    Note over Script,TokenService: Escalation Request: Workspace or Server\n    Script->>Gate: Request Escalated Scope (WORKSPACE or SERVER)\n    Gate->>Admin: Display Unmissable Blast Radius Warning Banner\n    Admin->>Gate: Cryptographic Signature with AAL2 Confirmation\n    Gate->>TokenService: Mint Time-Limited Ephemeral Escalated Token\n    TokenService-->>Script: Deliver Ephemeral Token for Execution\n```\n\n1. **Ephemeral Project Tokens:** By default, every script executes using an ephemeral API token scoped strictly to the current **Project**. It cannot read data from other projects or workspace settings.\n2. **Cryptographic Privilege Escalation:** If a script requires broader access (such as reading data across the entire **Workspace** or querying **Server** configuration):\n   - The script must request an escalated token scope.\n   - The UI displays an unmissable administrative warning banner detailing the blast radius.\n   - The escalation must be signed with cryptographic approval by an administrator possessing authority over that target tier.\n   - Scripts can never escalate to Server Admin privileges without explicit multi-factor confirmation.\n\n![Custom Fields Dual Control Escalation Studio](images/slice5-custom-fields-escalation-dual-control-desktop-1440x900-light.png)\n![Custom Fields Dual Control Escalation Flow](images/52-custom-fields-dual-control.png)\n\n### Dual-Control Principle:\nTo satisfy enterprise SOC 2 and ISO 27001 separation of duties, escalating a custom scripted field to workspace-wide or server-wide scope requires dual-control authorization:\n- A project administrator can author and propose the escalation.\n- A distinct, independent administrator holding target tier authority must review the blast radius warning banner and supply fresh Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2) credentials to activate the escalated token scope.\n- All escalation grants are logged with SHA-256 cryptographic digests in the immutable audit ledger.\n"
